 "notes": [
  "Corrected prevalence for a year = sum over the five model-stance labels of (share of that year's records with the model label) x (share of validation records with that model label that the coder assigned the target label) ({{N:note_correction_estimator}}). Target labels: Advocacy; critical (Alarm or Caution). Corpus: 14,058 records, 2021-2025.",
  "Constant rates (prespecified): rates from all 300 stance-validation records, applied to every year; records the coder judged not codable or out of scope count as human Neutral, as in {{T:stance_confusion}}. 95% CIs: 1000 bootstrap draws (seed 42) resampling validation records within model label and corpus records jointly. These are the estimates reported in the Results.",
  "Period-specific rates (post hoc): rates estimated separately from the 253 validation records published 2021-2023 or 2024-2025 (46 dated 2026 and 1 dated 2020 excluded) and applied to the years of the same period. 95% CIs: 1000 bootstrap draws (seed 42) resampling validation records within model label and period and corpus records jointly, with a Jeffreys Beta(k+1/2, n-k+1/2) draw for cells with no or all events. The validation sample was stratified by model stance, not by year, so period cells are small; * marks the one cell with fewer than 10 records.",
  "(b) and (c): exact Clopper-Pearson 95% CIs; Fisher exact two-sided test of the period difference within each model label. 'All years' uses all 300 validation records, including the 47 dated outside 2021-2025 (counts from {{T:stance_confusion}}). Precision: share of model-Advocacy records the coder labelled Advocacy; recall: share of coder-Advocacy records the model labelled Advocacy; in scope: the 225 records the coder judged codable and in scope.",
  "The post hoc analysis followed a written plan committed to the repository before it was run ({{N:note_data_code}}). Critical stance was Alarm or Caution."
 ],
